<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Monday 110,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Monday 110,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts were 110,000 head, compared with 108,000 a week ago and 105,000 a year ago. Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs.</p>
<p>Barrows and gilts were generally steady with the midsession Friday. Trade, demand and offerings moderate.</p>
<p>				  Country		    Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    54.50 -55.50	   55.50 -56.50</p>
<p>few			54.00  56.00	   55.00  57.00</p>
<p>few limited interest	  56.50		    57.50</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    53.50 -55.50	   54.00 -56.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    53.50 -55.50	   54.00 -56.50</p>
<p>Sows:  uneven, generally steady.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs   41.00 -45.00	   41.00 -45.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs	    43.00  47.00	   44.00  47.00</p>
<p>500 lbs-up	     45.00 -49.00	   46.00 -50.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct. carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
